---
import site from "../data/site.json";
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Hero from "../components/Hero.astro";
import DeckFigure from "../components/DeckFigure.astro";
import Citation from "../components/Citation.astro";
import { asset } from "../data/paths";
---
<Layout title={site.title} bare>
  <Hero />
  <div class="container visual-overview">
    <section class="section deck-section" id="background" aria-labelledby="background-title">
      <h2 id="background-title">Background</h2>
      <p class="deck-lead">Traffic congestion costs U.S. drivers billions of dollars a year. Autonomous driving offers a way to ease it: reinforcement learning (RL) can reduce collisions and move more vehicles through intersections.</p>
      <figure class="rv-spectrum">
        <div class="rv-ends">
          <DeckFigure id="human-vehicle" />
          <DeckFigure id="robot-vehicle" />
        </div>
        <div class="rv-bar" aria-hidden="true"></div>
        <figcaption class="rv-labels">
          <span><strong>Human traffic</strong>0% robot vehicles (RVs)</span>
          <span class="rv-mixed"><strong>Mixed traffic</strong></span>
          <span><strong>Robot traffic</strong>100% RVs</span>
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
    </section>

    <section class="section deck-section" id="method" aria-labelledby="method-title">
      <h2 id="method-title">Methodology</h2>
      <p class="deck-lead">We study a 14-intersection road network in Colorado Springs, Colorado, where human-driven and robot vehicles share the road, and compare our mixed-control framework with traffic-signal control.</p>
      <div class="network-compare wide-media">
        <DeckFigure id="prior-work" tag="Prior work" />
        <span class="compare-arrow" aria-hidden="true">⇄</span>
        <div class="network-ours">
          <DeckFigure id="network" tag="Ours" />
          <div class="tool-logos"><span>Built with</span><img src={asset("figures/deck/google-earth.webp")} width="480" height="112" alt="Google Earth" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /><img src={asset("figures/deck/sumo.webp")} width="200" height="200" alt="SUMO" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="deck-step">
        <h3>Robot vehicles choose Stop or Go</h3>
        <p>Near an intersection, each robot vehicle switches from the Intelligent Driver Model, which also drives the human vehicles, to an RL policy, trained with Rainbow DQN, that reads local traffic.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="method-slide"><DeckFigure id="method" /></div>
    </section>

    <section class="section deck-section" id="experiment" aria-label="Experiment">
      <p class="deck-lead">At a signalized intersection (S), traffic lights decide when vehicles go. An unsignalized intersection (U) has no lights: robot vehicles decide when to stop or go, and the human-driven vehicles behind them follow.</p>
      <div class="media-pair wide-media intersection-pair">
        <DeckFigure id="signalized" tag="Signalized (S)" />
        <DeckFigure id="unsignalized" tag="Unsignalized (U)" />
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section deck-section" id="results" aria-labelledby="results-title">
      <h2 id="results-title">Results</h2>
      <p class="deck-lead">With 80% robot vehicles and 8 of the 14 intersections unsignalized, the average wait falls from 6.17 to 5.09 seconds, and 493 vehicles reach their destinations every 500 seconds, up from 454 under traffic lights alone.</p>
      <div class="result-chart wide-media"><DeckFigure id="results-penetration" /></div>
      <p class="deck-lead result-follow">Gains differ by intersection. Choosing the best setup for each one, robot vehicles cut waiting at 9 of the 14 intersections when they make up half of traffic, and at 11 when they make up 80%.</p>
      <div class="result-chart wide-media result-scroll" role="region" tabindex="0" aria-label="Waiting time by intersection, horizontally scrollable on small screens">
        <div class="result-scroll-inner">
          <p class="chart-labels" aria-hidden="true"><span>50% robot vehicles</span><span>80% robot vehicles</span></p>
          <DeckFigure id="results-intersections" />
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section deck-section" id="conclusion" aria-labelledby="conclusion-title">
      <h2 id="conclusion-title">Conclusion</h2>
      <p class="deck-lead">Robot vehicles can take over intersections from traffic lights one step at a time. In a city-scale simulation, mixing unsignalized and signalized intersections shortened waits and moved more vehicles, a gradual path from traffic signals to autonomous intersection management.</p>
    </section>
    <Citation />
  </div>
</Layout>
